Description: CVE-2026-53795 - confine cross-tree operator-path syscalls against symlink-race link following
 rsync re-resolves a full pathname on each local rename / hard-link / basis
 open.  An attacker who can flip a parent component of a destination-tree path
 into a symlink (an absolute --temp-dir temp file, a --link-dest basis, or a
 malicious pull server's peer-selected --partial-dir basis) can redirect the
 tmp->final rename, the hard-link create, or the basis open outside the
 destination tree, yielding arbitrary file write, content injection, or an
 out-of-tree read leak (CWE-59).
 .
 The upstream 3.5.0 fix (commits a701236c and cfd40f55) confines these sinks
 with an fd-based ownership walk built on the secure_relative_open() /
 owner_walk_parent() / operator_path_resolve machinery introduced across
 3.4.0-3.4.3.  This package's rsync-3.2.3 tree already carries an equivalent,
 self-contained backport of that machinery (secure_relative_open(),
 do_open_nofollow(), do_rename_at(), do_link_at()) applied throughout
 syscall.c/generator.c/receiver.c/rsync.c/util.c by the prior
 CVE-2026-29518+43617+43618+43619+43620 patch series, so the tmp->final
 rename (util.c robust_rename, rsync.c finish_transfer) and the --link-dest
